#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the general formulation of quantum information, operations on quantum states are represented by a special class of mappings called *channels*.\n"
"This includes useful operations, such as ones corresponding to unitary gates and circuits, as well as operations we deem as noise and would prefer to avoid.\n"
"We can also describe measurements as channels, which we'll do in the next lesson.\n"
"In short, any <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A discrete-time change refers to one occurring between two distinct moments in time, as opposed to a continuous process that can be described over infinitesimally small time periods.\">discrete-time</DefinitionTooltip> change in states that is physically realizable (in an idealized sense) can be described by a channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam formulasi umum maklumat kuantum, operasi ke atas keadaan kuantum diwakili oleh kelas pemetaan khas yang dipanggil *saluran*.\n"
"Ini termasuk operasi yang berguna, seperti yang berpadanan dengan get uniter dan litar, serta operasi yang kita anggap sebagai hingar dan lebih suka dielakkan.\n"
"Kita juga boleh menerangkan pengukuran sebagai saluran, yang akan kita lakukan dalam pelajaran seterusnya.\n"
"Ringkasnya, sebarang perubahan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A discrete-time change refers to one occurring between two distinct moments in time, as opposed to a continuous process that can be described over infinitesimally small time periods.\">masa diskret</DefinitionTooltip> dalam keadaan yang boleh direalisasikan secara fizikal (dalam erti yang diidealisasikan) boleh diterangkan oleh saluran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The term *channel* comes to us from information theory, which (among other things) studies the information-carrying capacities of noisy *communication channels*.\n"
"In this context, a quantum channel could specify the quantum state that's received when a given quantum state is sent, perhaps through a quantum network of some sort.\n"
"It should be understood, however, that the terminology merely reflects this historical motivation and is used in a more general way.\n"
"Indeed, we can describe a wide variety of things (such as complicated quantum computations) as channels, even though they have nothing to do with communication and would be unlikely to arise naturally in such a setting.\n"
msgstr ""
"Istilah *saluran* datang kepada kita dari teori maklumat, yang (antara perkara lain) mengkaji kapasiti pembawa maklumat *saluran komunikasi* yang berhingar.\n"
"Dalam konteks ini, saluran kuantum boleh menentukan keadaan kuantum yang diterima apabila keadaan kuantum tertentu dihantar, mungkin melalui rangkaian kuantum tertentu.\n"
"Namun, harus difahami bahawa terminologi ini hanya mencerminkan motivasi sejarah dan digunakan dengan cara yang lebih umum.\n"
"Memang, kita boleh menerangkan pelbagai perkara (seperti pengiraan kuantum yang rumit) sebagai saluran, walaupun ia tidak ada kena-mengena dengan komunikasi dan tidak mungkin timbul secara semula jadi dalam tetapan sedemikian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll begin the lesson with a discussion of some basic aspects of channels, along with a small selection of examples.\n"
"Then we'll move on to three different ways to represent channels in mathematical terms later in the lesson.\n"
"We'll see that, although these representations are different, they all offer equivalent mathematical characterizations of channels.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan memulakan pelajaran dengan perbincangan tentang beberapa aspek asas saluran, berserta pilihan kecil contoh-contoh.\n"
"Kemudian kita akan beralih kepada tiga cara berbeza untuk mewakili saluran dalam sebutan matematik kemudian dalam pelajaran.\n"
"Kita akan melihat bahawa, walaupun perwakilan-perwakilan ini berbeza, semuanya menawarkan pencirian matematik saluran yang setara.\n"

